  "abstract": "We investigate the production of ultra-high-density matter (UHDM) in magnetically-dominated jets of active galactic nuclei (AGN) using general relativistic magnetohydrodynamic (GRMHD) simulations and effective field theory (EFT) calculations. Combining constraints from Fermi-LAT gamma-ray observations, IceCube neutrino detections, and Pierre Auger Observatory ultra-high-energy cosmic ray measurements, we perform a comprehensive Bayesian analysis of the UHDM parameter space. Our Monte Carlo analysis (10^6 samples) excludes UHDM masses in the range 100 GeV - 10 TeV for coupling strengths g > 0.1, assuming standard jet energetics. These results provide the most stringent multi-messenger constraints on exotic physics in AGN environments to date.",
